```

The original has two problems: a package-level mutable variable is shared, hidden global state that every caller of the package implicitly depends on (and that makes tests interfere with each other unless carefully reset), and it's not safe for concurrent use — two goroutines calling `Increment()` at the same time can race and lose an update. Wrapping the state in a struct with its own mutex makes ownership explicit (callers hold a `*Counter` instead of relying on package identity) and makes concurrent access safe.

